[h1]Tired of Manually Recruiting Prisoners in Your Court?[/h1]

Is your prison overflowing with potential courtiers, but recruiting each one (and demanding their conversion) manually feels like a chore? Look no further! This mod allows you to mass recruit and demand conversion from all non-ruler prisoners with a single click. You can even automate this process to run every month via an in-game decision.

[h2]Features:[/h2] [list] 
[*][b]Monthly Mass Actions[/b]:[list] 
[*][b]Mass Recruitment[/b]: Mass release/recruit prisoners based on your preferences of the vanilla options and a new prowess threshold. They must be willing to accept the terms, just like in the vanilla game.
[*][b]Mass Ransoming[/b]: Only prisoners that will give the maximum amout of gold/herd will be released.
[*][b]Note[/b]: The exclusion button from vanilla also works for the new mass actions.
[*][b]Note[/b]:  The adjusted bottom bar inside the prison with the new buttons for the mass actions will always be visible.
[*][b]Note[/b]:  Prisoners with whom you are at war or their close family will be excluded to prevent releasing relevant people for war score.
[/list] 
IMAGE TODO
[*][b]Mass Action Summaries and Stats inside Prison[/b]: You will be told how many people were ransomed/recruited/released and how much gold/herd you recieved.
IMAGE TODO
[*][b]Game Rule Personalization[/b]: You can personalize some stuff before starting the game.
[*][b]Inclusion and Adjustment of [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2790872361] Auto Demand Conversion [/url][/b]: Was not fixed for new update yet. If the author wishes me to remove it, i will do so. 
[*][b]Mass Torture Button[/b] : like requested in the comments 
[/list]

[h2]Important Details:[/h2] [list] 
[*][b]Visibility[/b]: The "Mass Action" button appears when you have 5 or more prisoners, similar to other mass actions in the game. 
[*][b]Game Rule Control[/b]: Enable or disable the mod features you want via a game rule.
[*][b]Choose what you want to do with your prisoners[/b]: Enable or disable each vanilla send option via a decision
 [/list]

